WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.238 --> 00:00:01.570
(paper airplane swooshing)

00:00:01.570 --> 00:00:03.277
(banging)

00:00:03.277 --> 00:00:04.228
- What's up believe nation?

00:00:04.228 --> 00:00:06.353
I started the Mentor Me
series to try to learn

00:00:06.353 --> 00:00:08.559
from people who've done a lot more than us

00:00:08.559 --> 00:00:10.830
and by hanging around
them a little bit longer,

00:00:10.830 --> 00:00:13.296
hopefully some of their
viewpoints, their mindset,

00:00:13.296 --> 00:00:15.623
their way of thinking
seeps into our brains

00:00:15.623 --> 00:00:18.632
to help us become the
best version of ourselves.

00:00:18.632 --> 00:00:20.469
Today we're going to
learn from Michelle Obama

00:00:20.469 --> 00:00:22.669
from some of her most inspiring moments.

00:00:22.669 --> 00:00:23.757
Mentor me, Michelle.

00:00:23.757 --> 00:00:25.143
Rule number two is my personal favorite,

00:00:25.143 --> 00:00:26.796
and I'm curious to figure out which one

00:00:26.796 --> 00:00:27.910
you guys like best.

00:00:27.910 --> 00:00:30.046
And as always guys, as
you're watching the videos,

00:00:30.046 --> 00:00:31.678
if you see something that really resonates

00:00:31.678 --> 00:00:33.369
with you, please leave it in the comments

00:00:33.369 --> 00:00:35.301
below and put quotes
around it so other people

00:00:35.301 --> 00:00:37.515
can be inspired, and if you write it down,

00:00:37.515 --> 00:00:40.929
it's much more likely to
stick with yourself as well.

00:00:40.929 --> 00:00:44.096
(inspirational music)

00:00:54.130 --> 00:00:57.051
- When you are struggling, and you start

00:00:57.051 --> 00:01:01.205
thinking about giving up,
I want you to remember

00:01:01.205 --> 00:01:03.239
something that my
husband and I have talked

00:01:03.239 --> 00:01:05.784
about since we first started this journey

00:01:05.784 --> 00:01:09.698
nearly a decade ago,
something that has carried

00:01:09.698 --> 00:01:13.282
us through every moment
in this White House

00:01:13.282 --> 00:01:15.741
and every moment of our lives.

00:01:15.741 --> 00:01:17.908
That is the power of hope.

00:01:19.907 --> 00:01:23.702
The belief that something
better is always possible

00:01:23.702 --> 00:01:27.869
if you're willing to work
for it and fight for it.

00:01:29.159 --> 00:01:31.764
It is our fundamental
belief in our power of hope

00:01:31.764 --> 00:01:34.804
that has allowed us to
rise above the voices

00:01:34.804 --> 00:01:38.137
of doubt and division, of anger and fear

00:01:39.924 --> 00:01:42.358
that we have faced in our own lives

00:01:42.358 --> 00:01:45.432
and in the life of this country.

00:01:45.432 --> 00:01:47.590
Our hope that if we work
hard enough and believe

00:01:47.590 --> 00:01:52.067
in ourselves then we can
be whatever we dream,

00:01:52.067 --> 00:01:56.234
regardless of the limitations
that others may place on us.

00:01:57.306 --> 00:01:59.677
The hope that when people see us for who

00:01:59.677 --> 00:02:02.260
we truly are, maybe just maybe,

00:02:04.243 --> 00:02:07.480
they too will be inspired to rise

00:02:07.480 --> 00:02:09.901
to their best possible selves.

00:02:09.901 --> 00:02:13.944
Shoot, it's the hope of folks like my dad,

00:02:13.944 --> 00:02:16.557
who got up every day,
do his job at the city

00:02:16.557 --> 00:02:20.140
water plant, the hope
that one day his kids

00:02:21.147 --> 00:02:23.803
would go to college and have opportunities

00:02:23.803 --> 00:02:25.470
he never dreamed of.

00:02:26.592 --> 00:02:31.556
That's the kind of hope
that every single one of us,

00:02:31.556 --> 00:02:35.351
politicians, parents,
preachers, all of us,

00:02:35.351 --> 00:02:38.331
need to be providing for our young people

00:02:38.331 --> 00:02:40.406
because that is what
moves this country forward

00:02:40.406 --> 00:02:44.144
every single day, our hope for the future

00:02:44.144 --> 00:02:46.525
and the hard work that hope inspires.

00:02:46.525 --> 00:02:50.647
Want our young people to
know that they matter,

00:02:50.647 --> 00:02:53.730
that they belong, so don't be afraid.

00:02:55.886 --> 00:02:56.719
You hear me?

00:02:56.719 --> 00:02:58.193
Young people, don't be afraid.

00:02:58.193 --> 00:02:59.110
Be focused.

00:03:00.537 --> 00:03:02.312
Be determined.

00:03:02.312 --> 00:03:03.890
Be hopeful.

00:03:03.890 --> 00:03:04.973
Be empowered.

00:03:05.847 --> 00:03:08.770
Empower yourselves with a good education,

00:03:08.770 --> 00:03:11.035
then get out there and use that education

00:03:11.035 --> 00:03:14.825
to build a country worthy
of your boundless promise.

00:03:14.825 --> 00:03:17.992
Lead by example with hope, never fear,

00:03:20.301 --> 00:03:22.850
and know that I will be with you,

00:03:22.850 --> 00:03:24.625
rooting for you and working to support you

00:03:24.625 --> 00:03:27.051
for the rest of my life.

00:03:27.051 --> 00:03:29.961
And that is true, I know, for every person

00:03:29.961 --> 00:03:33.908
who is here today and for
educators and advocates

00:03:33.908 --> 00:03:36.607
all across this nation
who get up every day

00:03:36.607 --> 00:03:40.323
and work their hearts out
to lift up our young people.

00:03:40.323 --> 00:03:44.757
I am so grateful to all
of you for your passion

00:03:44.757 --> 00:03:47.599
and your dedication and all the hard work

00:03:47.599 --> 00:03:50.083
on behalf of our next
generation, and I can

00:03:50.083 --> 00:03:52.989
think of no better way
to end my time as first

00:03:52.989 --> 00:03:56.885
lady than celebrating with all of you.

00:03:56.885 --> 00:04:00.732
I want to close today by
simply saying thank you.

00:04:00.732 --> 00:04:03.301
Thank you for everything
you do for our kids

00:04:03.301 --> 00:04:05.653
and for our counry.

00:04:05.653 --> 00:04:07.328
Being your first lady
has been the greatest

00:04:07.328 --> 00:04:11.411
honor of my life, and I
hope I've made you proud.

00:05:42.676 --> 00:05:45.337
Are you going to throw
up your hands and say

00:05:45.337 --> 00:05:47.571
that progress will never come?

00:05:47.571 --> 00:05:50.654
Are you going to get angry and lash out?

00:05:51.884 --> 00:05:54.807
Are you going to turn
inward and just give in

00:05:54.807 --> 00:05:57.057
to despair and frustration?

00:05:58.116 --> 00:06:00.873
Or are you going to take a deep breath,

00:06:00.873 --> 00:06:03.057
straighten your shoulders,
lift up your head

00:06:03.057 --> 00:06:05.517
and do what Barack Obama has always done

00:06:05.517 --> 00:06:09.017
as he says, "When they go low, I go high."

00:06:10.644 --> 00:06:14.061
That's the choice Barack and I have made.

00:06:14.950 --> 00:06:18.788
That's what has kept
us sane over the years.

00:06:18.788 --> 00:06:22.490
We simply do not allow
space in our hearts,

00:06:22.490 --> 00:06:24.823
minds or souls for darkness.

00:06:26.720 --> 00:06:28.803
Instead, we choose faith.

00:06:30.617 --> 00:06:33.294
Faith in ourselves and
the power of hard work.

00:06:33.294 --> 00:06:37.220
Faith in our God, whose overwhelming love

00:06:37.220 --> 00:06:40.039
sustains us every single day.

00:06:40.039 --> 00:06:41.872
That's what we choose.

00:06:43.467 --> 00:06:44.717
We choose love,

00:06:46.283 --> 00:06:48.743
our love for our children,

00:06:48.743 --> 00:06:51.558
our commitment to leaving
them a better world.

00:06:51.558 --> 00:06:54.357
Our love for our country,
which has given us

00:06:54.357 --> 00:06:57.123
so many blessings and advantages.

00:06:57.123 --> 00:06:59.517
Our love for our fellow citizens,

00:06:59.517 --> 00:07:03.023
parents workin' hard
to support their kids,

00:07:03.023 --> 00:07:04.842
men and women in uniform who risk

00:07:04.842 --> 00:07:07.092
everything to keep us safe.

00:07:07.993 --> 00:07:10.394
Young people from the toughest backgrounds

00:07:10.394 --> 00:07:13.160
who never stop believing in their dreams.

00:07:13.160 --> 00:07:15.611
Young people like so many of you.

00:07:15.611 --> 00:07:17.444
That's what we choose,

00:07:18.580 --> 00:07:20.663
and we choose excellence.

00:07:22.082 --> 00:07:23.957
We choose to tune out all the noise

00:07:23.957 --> 00:07:28.404
and strive for excellence
in everything we do.

00:07:28.404 --> 00:07:31.873
No cuttin' corners, no
takin' shortcuts, no whining.

00:07:31.873 --> 00:07:36.040
We give 120% every single
time because excellence,

00:07:36.972 --> 00:07:40.777
excellence is the most powerful answer

00:07:40.777 --> 00:07:43.576
you can give to the
doubters and the haters.

00:07:43.576 --> 00:07:46.576
(audience cheering)

00:07:48.142 --> 00:07:51.603
It's also the most powerful thing you can

00:07:51.603 --> 00:07:55.855
do for yourself, see 'cause
the process of striving

00:07:55.855 --> 00:07:59.671
and strugglin' and pushing
yourself to new heights,

00:07:59.671 --> 00:08:03.488
see that's how you develop
your God-given talents.

00:08:03.488 --> 00:08:06.479
That's how you make yourself
stronger and smarter

00:08:06.479 --> 00:08:09.817
and more able to make a
difference for others.

00:08:09.817 --> 00:08:13.699
Next, I've always felt a
deep sense of obligation

00:08:13.699 --> 00:08:16.583
to make the biggest
impact possible with this

00:08:16.583 --> 00:08:19.677
incredible platform, so
I took on issues that

00:08:19.677 --> 00:08:21.884
were personal to me.

00:08:21.884 --> 00:08:25.641
Issues like helping families
raise healthier kids,

00:08:25.641 --> 00:08:27.906
honoring the incredible military families

00:08:27.906 --> 00:08:29.995
that I've met out on the campaign trail,

00:08:29.995 --> 00:08:33.232
inspiring our young people
to value their education

00:08:33.232 --> 00:08:34.901
and finish college.

00:08:34.901 --> 00:08:36.408
(audience applauding)

00:08:36.408 --> 00:08:39.828
Now, some folks criticized
my choices for not

00:08:39.828 --> 00:08:44.110
being bold enough, but
these were my choices,

00:08:44.110 --> 00:08:47.386
my issues, and I decided
to tackle them in a way

00:08:47.386 --> 00:08:50.002
that felt most authentic to me.

00:08:50.002 --> 00:08:53.803
In a way that was both
substantive and strategic

00:08:53.803 --> 00:08:56.260
but also fun and hopefully inspiring,

00:08:56.260 --> 00:08:59.064
so I immersed myself
in the policy details.

00:08:59.064 --> 00:09:01.146
I worked with Congress on legislation,

00:09:01.146 --> 00:09:04.330
gave speeches to CEOs, military generals,

00:09:04.330 --> 00:09:07.090
Hollywood executives, but
I also worked to ensure

00:09:07.090 --> 00:09:10.555
that my efforts would resonate
with kids and families,

00:09:10.555 --> 00:09:12.515
and that meant doing things in a creative

00:09:12.515 --> 00:09:14.368
and unconventional way.

00:09:14.368 --> 00:09:17.271
So yeah, I planted a
garden and hula-hooped

00:09:17.271 --> 00:09:19.068
on the White House lawn with kids.

00:09:19.068 --> 00:09:21.820
I did some mom dancing on TV.

00:09:21.820 --> 00:09:25.214
I celebrated military
kids with Kermit the Frog.

00:09:25.214 --> 00:09:27.028
I asked folks across the country to wear

00:09:27.028 --> 00:09:31.427
their alma mater's T-shirts
for college signing day.

00:09:31.427 --> 00:09:35.299
And at the end of the day, by staying true

00:09:35.299 --> 00:09:38.901
to the me I've always
known, I found that this

00:09:38.901 --> 00:09:41.818
journey has been incredibly freeing

00:09:42.690 --> 00:09:45.631
because no matter what happened,
I had the peace of mind

00:09:45.631 --> 00:09:49.317
of knowing that all of the
chatter, the name-calling,

00:09:49.317 --> 00:09:52.669
the doubting, all of it was just noise.

00:09:52.669 --> 00:09:53.525
(audience applauding)

00:09:53.525 --> 00:09:55.739
It did not define me.

00:09:55.739 --> 00:09:58.393
It didn't change who I was,

00:09:58.393 --> 00:10:02.625
and most importantly, it
couldn't hold me back.

00:10:02.625 --> 00:10:04.808
I have learned that as long as I hold fast

00:10:04.808 --> 00:10:07.520
to my beliefs and values and follow my own

00:10:07.520 --> 00:10:10.911
moral compass, then
the only expectations I

00:10:10.911 --> 00:10:14.017
need to live up to are my own.

00:10:14.017 --> 00:10:17.565
We want our children and
all children in this nation

00:10:17.565 --> 00:10:19.938
to know that the only limit to the height

00:10:19.938 --> 00:10:22.732
of your achievements is
the reach of your dreams

00:10:22.732 --> 00:10:25.477
and your willingness
to work hard for them.

00:10:25.477 --> 00:10:28.401
(audience applauding)

00:10:28.401 --> 00:10:31.782
And as our friendship grew, and I learned

00:10:31.782 --> 00:10:35.634
more about Barack, he
introduced me to the work

00:10:35.634 --> 00:10:39.533
that he'd done when he first
moved to Chicago after college.

00:10:39.533 --> 00:10:42.469
You see, instead of going to Wall Street,

00:10:42.469 --> 00:10:46.485
Barack went to work in
neighborhoods that had

00:10:46.485 --> 00:10:50.516
been devastated by the
closing of steel plants.

00:10:50.516 --> 00:10:53.768
Jobs dried up, and Barack was invited back

00:10:53.768 --> 00:10:56.366
to speak to people from
those neighborhoods

00:10:56.366 --> 00:10:58.927
about how to rebuild their community.

00:10:58.927 --> 00:11:01.493
And the people gathered
there together that day

00:11:01.493 --> 00:11:04.877
were ordinary folks
doing the best they could

00:11:04.877 --> 00:11:06.510
to build a good life.

00:11:06.510 --> 00:11:09.863
See, they were parents tryin' to get by

00:11:09.863 --> 00:11:11.856
from paycheck to paycheck.

00:11:11.856 --> 00:11:15.043
Grandparents tryin' to get it
together on a fixed income.

00:11:15.043 --> 00:11:17.973
Men frustrated that they couldn't support

00:11:17.973 --> 00:11:20.985
their families after jobs had disappeared.

00:11:20.985 --> 00:11:22.655
You see, those folks weren't asking

00:11:22.655 --> 00:11:24.890
for a handout or a shortcut.

00:11:24.890 --> 00:11:26.922
They were ready to work.

00:11:26.922 --> 00:11:28.714
They wanted to contribute.

00:11:28.714 --> 00:11:31.049
They believed, like you
and I believe, that America

00:11:31.049 --> 00:11:34.825
should be a place where
you can make it if you try.

00:11:34.825 --> 00:11:37.992
(audience applauding)

00:11:39.659 --> 00:11:44.149
And Barack stood up that
day, and he spoke words

00:11:44.149 --> 00:11:47.347
that have stayed with me ever since.

00:11:47.347 --> 00:11:50.180
He talked about the world as it is

00:11:51.059 --> 00:11:53.258
and the world as it should be,

00:11:53.258 --> 00:11:55.801
and he said that all too often we accept

00:11:55.801 --> 00:11:58.676
the distance between
the two, and we settle

00:11:58.676 --> 00:12:00.933
for the world as it is,
even when it doesn't

00:12:00.933 --> 00:12:04.047
reflect our values and aspirations.

00:12:04.047 --> 00:12:07.464
But he reminded us that we also know what

00:12:08.298 --> 00:12:10.682
the world should look like.

00:12:10.682 --> 00:12:13.513
He said, "We know what
fairness and justice

00:12:13.513 --> 00:12:17.324
"and opportunity look
like," and he urged us

00:12:17.324 --> 00:12:19.933
to believe in ourselves,
to find the strength

00:12:19.933 --> 00:12:23.821
within ourselves to strive
for the world as it should be.

00:12:23.821 --> 00:12:26.727
And isn't that the great American story?

00:12:26.727 --> 00:12:30.106
(audience cheering)

00:12:30.106 --> 00:12:33.357
It's the story of men and women gathered

00:12:33.357 --> 00:12:37.088
in churches and union
halls, in high school gyms

00:12:37.088 --> 00:12:40.557
and people who stood up
and marched and risked

00:12:40.557 --> 00:12:43.872
everything they had, refusing to settle,

00:12:43.872 --> 00:12:46.151
determined to mold our future

00:12:46.151 --> 00:12:48.751
into the shape of our ideals.

00:12:48.751 --> 00:12:50.035
- Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:12:50.035 --> 00:12:52.066
I'd love to know what did
you think of this video?

00:12:52.066 --> 00:12:53.763
What did you learn from
Michelle that you're

00:12:53.763 --> 00:12:55.543
going to immediately apply to your life

00:12:55.543 --> 00:12:56.913
or your business somehow?

00:12:56.913 --> 00:12:58.535
Please leave it down
in the comments below,

00:12:58.535 --> 00:13:00.202
and I'm going to join in the discussion.

00:13:00.202 --> 00:13:02.230
I also want to give a quick
shout-out to Cristi Vlad.

00:13:02.230 --> 00:13:03.719
Cristi, thank you so much for picking up

00:13:03.719 --> 00:13:06.578
a copy of my book, Your
One Word, and posting

00:13:06.578 --> 00:13:09.314
that YouTube video review on your channel.

00:13:09.314 --> 00:13:11.723
I really, really, really
appreciate the support.

00:13:11.723 --> 00:13:13.787
- [Cristi] I'm going
to tell you about a few

00:13:13.787 --> 00:13:16.551
insights that I got from Evan Carmichael's

00:13:16.551 --> 00:13:18.134
book Your One Word.

00:13:19.374 --> 00:13:20.674
So thank you guys again for watching.

00:13:20.674 --> 00:13:22.007
I believe in you.

00:13:22.007 --> 00:13:23.774
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:13:23.774 --> 00:13:25.878
and whatever your one word is.

00:13:25.878 --> 00:13:28.450
Much love, I'll see you soon.

00:13:28.450 --> 00:13:30.930
(swooshing and banging)

